(A) van't Hoff factor $i = \frac{\text{Normal molar mass}}{\text{Abnormal molar mass}}$ (III);
(B) $k_f =$ Cryoscopic constant (I);
(C) Solutions with same osmotic pressure are isotonic solutions (II);
(D) Azeotropes are constant boiling mixtures with same composition in liquid and vapour phases (IV).

(A) Chloroform and acetone show negative deviation from Raoult's law $\rightarrow$ Maximum boiling azeotrope (III);
(B) Ethanol and water show positive deviation $\rightarrow$ Minimum boiling azeotrope (I);
(C) Benzene and toluene form an ideal solution $\rightarrow \Delta V_{\text{mix}} = 0$ (IV);
(D) Acetic acid in benzene undergoes intermolecular hydrogen bonding and dimerizes (II).
